% tokens (closed-world sort checking)
a: type.
b: type.
c: type.
d: type.
k: bin -> type.

% Ample-set completeness for TIMELESS outputs (THY_0025 condition (ii)):
% mk_k has delay 5, but its PERSISTENT output !k 1 is produced at fire
% time (the persistent zone carries no stamps) — it enables `need` at the
% SAME instant. {mk_k, grab} share no cohort, yet the firing order decides
% whether `need` ever exists: mk_k-first forks {grab, need} on cohort b
% (c-world vs d-world); grab-first reaches only the c-world. An explore
% that returns false from the delay check before looking at persistent
% consequents commits one order and misses the d-world.

mk_k: a -o { !k 1 }@5.
grab: b -o { c }@1.
need: b * !k 1 -o { d }@1.
